review.claim:
armTaxes schedules Tax Season every 1 February at 09:00 New York time and re-arms it each year. The handler:
- settles UK years that fell due on 31 January;
- skips a year owesUsReturn says the US doesn't tax;
- works out figuresFor(the year before);
- makes returns[year], due 15 April (or the 1040-NR's date);
- schedules TAX_DUE at the due date;
- asks the player 'Your <year> Tax Return' with File It (tax.file).
Its own comment says a year with nothing owed and nothing due back gets no return.

At the due date of an unfiled return:
- if it owes the IRS, the IRS's substitute is proposed at due + 365 days (TAX_SFR);
- each state owed gets its non-filer letters (scheduleStateNonFiler);
- Oregon's three-year check is set;
- the player is told 'Your <year> Return Is Late': 5% a month to a quarter, at least $525 past 60 days, or 'A refund waits'.
